==============================================================================
                          DATA PACKET STRUCTURE
==============================================================================

Telemetry Packet (ASCII Format):
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ WQM | 123 | 1845 | 7.2 | 15.5 | 18.3 | 37.7749 | -122.4194 | ... │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  │     │     │      │     │      │       │          │
  │     │     │      │     │      │       │          └─ Longitude
  │     │     │      │     │      │       └─ Latitude
  │     │     │      │     │      └─ Temperature (°C)
  │     │     │      │     └─ Turbidity (NTU)
  │     │     │      └─ pH Value
  │     │     └─ System Uptime (seconds)
  │     └─ Packet ID (sequential)
  └─ Header ("Water Quality Monitor")

SD Card Log Entry (CSV Format):
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Timestamp, pH, Turbidity, Temp, Lat, Lon, Alt, Sats, Battery      │
│ 1705334400, 7.2, 15.5, 18.3, 37.774900, -122.419400, 0.5, 10, 95 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

==============================================================================
                            DATA FLOW RATES
==============================================================================

Sensor Sampling:
- pH: Continuous (averaged over 10 samples)
- Turbidity: Continuous (averaged over 10 samples)
- Temperature: 1Hz (DS18B20 conversion time ~750ms)
- GPS: 10Hz (position updates)

Data Logging:
- SD Card: Every 5 seconds (CSV append)
- LoRa TX: Every 10 seconds (complete packet)
- Real-time Display: Upon reception

Data Volumes (Typical 20-minute mission):
- SD Card Log: ~240 entries × 100 bytes = 24 KB
- LoRa Telemetry: ~120 packets × 80 bytes = 9.6 KB
- Total Data: ~30-50 KB per mission

==============================================================================

To create actual PNG diagram:
1. Use draw.io or similar tool
2. Create flowchart with swim lanes
3. Color-code by system (UAV, Sensors, GCS)
4. Add icons for components
5. Export as high-resolution PNG
6. Save to this location

